@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Front matter and cross-references)

Authors, abstract, keywords, notes, labels and references to them.

@section(Front matter)

@subsection(@@author)

One author line — name, department, affiliation, email.

@author(name=Alex Rivera, department=Physics, affiliation=Example University)

@author(name=Sam Okafor, department=Chemistry, affiliation=Example University, email=s.okafor@example.edu)

@subsection(@@authors)

Authors pulled from author.db by id; style=full\|names\|short\|ieee\|email, or anon for blind review.

@authors(dk, sg)

@authors(dk, sg, style=ieee)

@subsection(@@author_cr)

An author credit line from author.db: each name links to the generated Authors page with photo, contact and every other field.

@author_cr(dk, sg)

@subsection(@@anonymous)

Blind review: replace every author with Author 1, Author 2…

@anonymous

@subsection(@@abstract)

The paper abstract block.

@abstract
The summary.
@end

@subsection(@@keywords)

Paper keywords — IEEE prints them as Index Terms.

@keywords(fpga, timing)

@subsection(@@indexterms)

Index terms for a paper (IEEE prints them as Index Terms).

@indexterms(fpga, timing)

@subsection(@@note)

A numbered note block.

@note … @end

@section(Labels and references)

@subsection(@@label)

Attach a label to the thing above so ref/eqref/qref can point at it.

@label(fig1)

@subsection(@@ref)

Reference labelled figures, tables, sections, equations or theorems: one, or several ("Figures 1 and 2"), or the page one is on.

@ref(fig1, fig2)

@ref(fig1, tab3)
on @ref(fig1, page)

@subsection(@@qref)

Reference a labelled question — prints its number ("Q3").
